  "query_preview": "..\nAs Jangmi lifts north-northwestward, showers continue to build \nacross the converging monsoon and trade-wind patterns. Latest model \nand satellite trends indicate intermittent breaks in showers activity\nacross the Marianas due to the disorganized pattern. Still, outflow \nboundaries from the nearby monsoon pattern and a nocturnal boost in \nshowers may still bring an increase in showers overnight. Locally \nheavy showers remain possible through Thursday and isolated \nthunderstorms persist through Thursday night for Tinian and Saipan \nand through Friday or Friday night for Guam and Rota. Over the \nweekend, showers are expected to trend down to isolated as the \ntrailing convergence from Jangmi shifts off to the west. However, an \nunsettled pattern remains nearby across western Micronesia, possibly \nbringing a slight uptick in showers across Guam and Rota.",
